WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.620
Citadel starts with one command: slash do.

2
00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:07.890
Describe the engineering outcome, and Citadel chooses the smallest operating lane that can carry it.

3
00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:15.730
Longer work gains repository state, recovery, coordination, bounded execution, and a concrete next action around Claude Code or Codex.

4
00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.420
The research question begins where orchestration ends.

5
00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:25.220
A smaller model is not cheaper when its answer fails, verification forces a retry, or the operation hides part of its cost.

6
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:33.740
Citadel binds the declared route to observed execution, a deterministic verdict outside the routed model, measured and modeled cost lenses, and a signed receipt.

7
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.330
Failed and unknown outcomes remain visible.

8
00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.490
Three local studies tested that contract.

9
00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:43.760
In v1, adaptive recorded twenty-seven of thirty-six verified cells versus twenty-four.

10
00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.140
But one same-route sixty-second baseline timeout drove the apparent savings.

11
00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:52.880
Excluding that pair reverses the economic direction, so Citadel makes no savings claim.

12
00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:57.230
V2 tested one-point-five, three, and seven-billion-parameter routing.

13
00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:02.270
It matched baseline cell completion, but twelve failed small-model attempts escalated to seven B.

14
00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:05.960
The policy used fifteen point seven percent more GPU energy.

15
00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.210
Citadel rejected it.

16
00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:11.940
V3 moved from exact answers to six artifact-producing repository fixtures.

17
00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.420
Both policies verified six of twelve cells.

18
00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:23.590
Citadel recorded zero false passes and zero path violations, but its seven point one percent energy reduction missed the frozen twenty percent gate, and token use increased.

19
00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:25.660
That result is also published as failed.

20
00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:29.030
This is the point: Citadel does not let a router grade itself.

21
00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:36.110
Sentient funding would scale this open operation-evidence layer across agent stacks, real repositories, model families, and hardware.

22
00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:45.530
The target remains at least eighty percent absolute verified completion, at least ninety-five percent of a valid frontier baseline, and at least thirty percent lower measured end-to-end cost.

23
00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:51.170
Frontier must first clear eighty percent overall and seventy percent in every frozen task stratum.

24
00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:56.850
Methods, receipts, commands, and negative results stay public whether that target passes or fails.
